cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal,
  work-in-progress synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI
  assistant by Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed,
  and not a new result.
title: "reader-ergonomics-blueprint (work in progress)"
abstract: >-
  A person's reasoning written as a tree of topics, with a checker on each
  part, Lean for logic first, and a language model that interprets the
  checkers' verdicts and guides. Its review of autoformalization is done and
  names its baseline; the loop itself is not built yet.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/reader-ergonomics-blueprint"
license:
